  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The reaction of alcohol with Lucas reagent is mostly an  <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow></msub><mn>1</mn></math>  mechanism reaction and the rate of reaction is directly proportional to the carbocation stability formed in the reaction, hence tertiary alcohol will react fastest.",
